%% ====== DIAGRAM RULES (STRUCTURAL GUARDRAILS) ======
%% These rules MUST be followed to maintain K0/K1/Bridge boundary integrity:
%%
%% R1: ALL EXTERNAL INGRESS MUST TERMINATE AT K0_BRIDGE
%%     ❌ NO direct ING→CMD/QRY/SSE/OBS edges allowed
%%     ✅ Clients → K0_BRIDGE → K0 Ports
%%
%% R2: P01–P20 PIPELINES MUST BE INSIDE K0_KERNEL
%%     ❌ NO external "Facade→K0 Bus" in user-space
%%     ✅ K0_BUS → P01-P20 → K0_DRIVERS (all within kernel)
%%
%% R3: NO USER-SPACE EDGES TO st_* DRIVERS/ALIASES
%%     ❌ NO cognition → st_sem/st_vec/st_fts direct access
%%     ✅ Writes: module → K0_BRIDGE → CMD
%%     ✅ Reads: module → K0_BRIDGE → QRY
%%
%% R4: K0_PEP@SYSCALL = ONLY AUTHORITY
%%     ❌ User-space PEP/QoS/Safety are HINTS only
%%     ✅ K0_PEP at syscall boundary is enforcement point
%%
%% R5: SSE SUBSCRIPTIONS TERMINATE AT BRIDGE
%%     ❌ NO direct app subscriptions to K0.SSE
%%     ✅ Apps → K0_BRIDGE → SSE Port
%%
